course: dictionary
lesson: 12807
title: Elite: the very best
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Elite means the very best, or the highest level. «Only the elite runners got through to the final.» The clue is the word final: only the best runners reach it, so elite runners are the best of all.
explain: As a noun, the elite is a small group of people at the top, such as people with the most skill, power or money. «The elite squad trained every morning before school.» Here the elite squad is a small team of the very best players. Elites is the plural and means more than one such group.
explain: Sometimes people use elite to complain. «Some people say the elite make rules that do not help ordinary families.» The clues are rules and ordinary families. The writer means rich, powerful people who seem out of touch with everyday life.
fact: Elite (adjective) means the very best or of the highest level.
fact: The elite (noun) is a small group of people who are the best, or who have the most power, money or importance.
fact: Phrases you may meet: elite athletes, elite teams, elite soldiers, elite schools.
fact: «The elite athletes trained every day for the big race.» Here the athletes are the very best.
fact: In a complaint, «the elite» can mean rich, powerful people who seem out of touch. Check the clues around the word to see which meaning is used.
exercise: «The elite athletes trained every day for the big race.» What does elite mean in this sentence? | Ordinary, like everyone else | *The very best | Lost and alone | Very old
exercise: Find the adjective in this sentence: «Elite teams train hard.» | *elite | teams | train | every
exercise: «Some people complain that the elite make rules that do not help ordinary families.» Why might someone use the word elite here? | *To criticise rich, powerful people who seem out of touch | To say the people are very young | To say the people are very tired | To say the rules are very short
test: «The elite soldiers crossed the river at night.» What does elite mean in this sentence? | *The best and most highly trained | Very noisy | Newly built | Sleepy
test: Which of these is an elite squad? | A pile of old books | A group of lost children | A list of rules for a game | *A small team of the best players
exam: «Only the elite are picked for the national team, so being chosen is a real honour.» What does the elite mean here? | Ordinary people | Tiny insects | *The best, the highest-level group | Lazy people
